Honestly, zen conduct is not that hard.  My strategy in brief: leave
pet on level one without killing it (for curse-identify later), skip
the mines (easier to find floating eyes in corridors than in wide
spaces) and proceed slowly until you find a floating eye.  (Giggle
maniacally when you die and realize you've killed three or four of
them and none left corpses.) Definitely never descend deeper than the
Oracle without telepathy.  Hordes of orcs or bees are...less than good
when totally blind and low level ;).  But, once you have a floating
eye corpse, zen samurai plays almost the same as a normal game.  The
biggest changes are no altar-BUC-identify (not terrible), no
definitive pet-curse-identify (annoying when you mis-think something
is non-cursed), and a nigh-requisite trip to a store before you can
use most items (tedious).  My stash in most games exists in a box in
the minetown general store.

